From d66e4bc62cb50590b8eefacb81ef6cb603f57796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:19:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Validate runtime registrations like a parsed graph (issue 7)

registerEdges, registerScreens and registerActions previously accepted
anything, so an unknown action type or a payload that breaks the schema got
through with no diagnostics.

- Per-item validation is split out of validateGraph into validateScreenRecord
  and validateEdgeRecord, so file and runtime items share one set of checks.
- Registration stages items, validates them (endpoints, schema action types,
  payloads, variable references, costs, conditions, metadata), then commits.
- Failures throw ValidationError with diagnostics and change nothing.
  { diagnostics: "collect" } registers the valid items and records the rest
  on tree.diagnostics.
- Unknown template, duplicate explicit edge id and bad conditions are now
  diagnostics instead of bare Errors.

